    "created_at": "2017-03-09T16:51:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-09T16:51:28Z",
    "body": "I don't think we should force implementations to catch and store allocation errors, only to shuttle them over to the destination, just to support a hypothetical copy-on-write future. It's simpler to allow allocation errors to bubble up where they occur, IMO. If someone does a copy-on-write version then they'll need to throw the error at write time, which could be arbitrarily later (not just at receive time).\r\n\r\nMy point above was that I at least didn't realize when allocation happened for the simple case like cloning (not tranferring) an array buffer.",
